Superchat development handoff — 2026-11-25

Changes made by Codex

- Restored the Superchat implementation and added Windows and Unix installation launchers.
- Fixed a sign-in callback race and serialized concurrent session refreshes.
- Fixed sessions created by email links where the token expiry was stored as a string. Existing sessions are accepted.
- Fixed a Windows MCP hang when resolving a project folder through Git.
- Updated capture instructions to request concise, distinct decisions and omit redundant optional fields.
- Limited embedding model threads and imported embedding dependencies before MCP worker threads start to address review-list hangs on Windows.
- Registered the local Superchat MCP with Claude Desktop, Claude Code, and Codex on the development computer. Those local registrations are not distributed by this log.

Verification

- The full suite passed 219 tests before the later focused fixes.
- Focused sign-in tests passed 45 tests; core, MCP, and agent tests passed 80 tests; and the latest MCP/core checks passed 38 tests.
- A live MCP keep test saved and removed a temporary draft using the existing Supabase session.
- A live MCP review-list test returned eight pending items in approximately five seconds. The interactive Claude review and Push flow still requires end-to-end validation.
- The Supabase project already contained the Superchat schema. Existing unrelated database functions were preserved.

Deployment notes

- The repository contains the editable Supabase project URL and publishable key as defaults. The local superchat.env file contains credentials and is ignored by Git.
- The embedding model is loaded locally. Initial installation or model download and availability can affect startup.
- Claude Desktop must be fully restarted, and Claude Code and Codex need new sessions, after changing their local MCP registrations.
- Installer launchers and the full live employee onboarding flow still require end-to-end testing on each target platform.

Review connection update

- Replaced the review tool's artifact-publishing instruction with an MCP App resource and a host-mediated MCP bridge. The review page requests the pending list and sends one Push through the same MCP server.
- A failed load no longer says there is nothing to review or displays a zero-item push as if loading succeeded.
- Tests cover MCP tool metadata, resource MIME type, the review page and a simulated MCP App host including Push. Claude Desktop's actual host rendering and Push remain to be verified with the user.

Plugin and review update — 2026-11-26

- Added a Claude Code plugin marketplace, plugin commands, MCP configuration and hook launcher. The launcher uses an existing virtual environment when possible and avoids blocking prompts on a failed environment lookup.
- The review tool returns its pending items in the initial MCP App result. In a live Claude Code GUI test, the review displayed a captured test item; this host reported that IPC for app-initiated MCP calls was unavailable, so the screen was read-only and Push remains unverified.
- Updated setup instructions to request a local Claude Code session and install the plugin from the repository. A cloud session cannot install on the user's computer.
